  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Going The Ways** (1 review, 1 other source): Reviewer singles out this song, which they say John wrote for his son; Uploader's notes list this song as unreleased on any album [1][2]\n- **Sixteen Tons (Merle Travis Cover)** (1 other source): Uploader's notes list this Merle Travis cover as unreleased on any album [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro Subsides-Waylon Jennings Live!**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Dutch Orchestra Blues**: back after 67 archived shows (1687 days) [4]\n- **In The Hidden Places**: back after 34 archived shows (616 days) [4]\n- **No More Tears**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Going To Jamaica**: back after 63 archived shows (1444 days) [4]\n- **Satanic Messiah**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Lakeside View Background**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Sixteen Tons (Merle Travis Cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2018-05-27** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 84 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the binaural audience recording crisp and immersive, best heard on headphones; Commenter says the recording sounds great [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Folk Music, Foreign Object [1]\n- Reviewer says Matt and John make a strong duo, with energy between them lifting the songs, in an intimate venue [2]\n- Commenter tried to record the second night but had a gear malfunction, so this recording is better than theirs [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2018-05-27**: taped by LMGBTapes; transferred by LMGBTapes; source: AUD (balcony) > CA-14 Omnidirectional Mics > CA-Ugly Battery Box > Zoom H4n Pro (@ 24bit/48khz, mic level 10) [1]",
